Files dropped here are used by the build instead of being downloaded (see the header of
../Dockerfile): for a build host that cannot reach download.opensuse.org or PyPI.  The directory is
otherwise empty; the files are not committed (.gitignore).

  zeek-9.0-core_<version>_<arch>.deb   https://download.opensuse.org/repositories/security:/zeek/Debian_13/<arch>/
  zeekctl-9.0_<version>_<arch>.deb     (same place)
  wheels/                              the wheels of cowrie==3.1.8 and of its dependencies, e.g. on
                                       any machine with pip:
      pip download -d wheels --only-binary=:all: --platform manylinux_2_28_x86_64 \
          --python-version 3.13 --implementation cp cowrie==3.1.8

Check the two .deb against the SHA256 of the Packages index of the repository (its Release file
is signed by the key whose fingerprint the Dockerfile checks), and the wheels against the hashes
PyPI publishes.
